WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.370
Imagine knowing that there’s a monster,
right under your nose.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:09.980
Imagine knowing that this monster is capable
of killing any human being on earth, and all

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:14.330
because they simply saw a photograph of its
face.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:19.179
When this monster is on the warpath, literally
nothing can stop it.

00:00:19.179 --> 00:00:24.499
No weapon that human beings have invented
is capable of even slowing it down.

00:00:24.499 --> 00:00:32.150
Imagine knowing, in the age of mass media,
of clicks and shares, of 24 hour news, smart

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:37.650
phones, and limitless social media connecting
billions across the globe, that one stray

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:42.970
picture of this monster leaked in the wrong
place could cause the end of the world as

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:44.440
we know it.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.380
And this fateful, terrifying day could come
at any time.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:55.790
Congratulations, you now know how it feels
to be Dr. Dan, the hot-headed lead SCP Foundation

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:59.960
researcher on the SCP-096 case.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:05.149
The anomaly itself requires no real introduction
- the infamous, mass-murdering Shy Guy has

00:01:05.149 --> 00:01:08.969
haunted the nightmares of Foundation experts
for years.

00:01:08.969 --> 00:01:14.560
But nobody is more haunted by this thing than
Dr. Dan himself.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:20.909
For over a decade now, he has firmly believed
that there’s one solution to the 096 problem:

00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:23.619
Termination, with extreme prejudice.

00:01:23.619 --> 00:01:28.960
In his eyes, to think that 096 is ever truly
contained is an illusion.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.249
They could never be sure of how many pictures
of it are out there, floating around just

00:01:33.249 --> 00:01:37.909
waiting to be seen, like a time bomb waiting
to go off.

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:43.030
The resources spent containing it and cleaning
up after its rampages, he would often argue,

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:47.329
would be better spent instead figuring out
how to finally kill it.

00:01:47.329 --> 00:01:52.649
But seeing as we’re talking about the SCP
Foundation here, not the Global Occult Coalition,

00:01:52.649 --> 00:01:56.649
the O5 Council didn’t see it quite the same
way.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:02:01.939
They constantly overturned Dr. Dan’s termination
requests, leaving the paranoid researcher

00:02:01.939 --> 00:02:04.670
more furious with each rejection.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:08.090
He tried to warn them, again and again and
again.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.259
“Don’t you see?

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:12.659
It’s like a stick of dynamite, and the fuse
is already lit.

00:02:12.659 --> 00:02:17.430
If you don’t let me put it out before it’s
too late, there won’t even be anyone left

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.080
to pick up the pieces!”

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.489
But his pleas fell on deaf ears.

00:02:21.489 --> 00:02:29.129
Until, of course, Incident 096-1-a, a dark
and bloody day still looked back on with shame

00:02:29.129 --> 00:02:33.689
and horror by even the most hardened members
of Foundation staff.

00:02:33.689 --> 00:02:40.330
It was the day that SCP-096 gave everyone
a taste of the mass carnage it was truly capable

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:41.330
of.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:44.620
Dr. Dan wasn’t even there when containment
was first breached.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:50.810
He was off on an expedition in the snowy mountains
where 096 was first found, trying to discover

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:52.750
clues to its true origin.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:58.660
Dr. Dan’s second in command, Dr. Oleksei,
was also lucky enough to be outside of the

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:01.579
containment area when the Shy Guy escaped.

00:03:01.579 --> 00:03:06.190
According to interviews he gave at debriefing
tribunals, he was in the break room, treating

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:08.890
himself to a warm cup of joe.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:14.040
All the other personnel assigned to 096’s
containment and research were near its containment

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:19.909
chamber, a giant cube made of reinforced metal,
observing a live feed of data being collected

00:03:19.909 --> 00:03:21.870
from the cube’s interior.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:26.099
As usual, sensors indicated that 096 was pacing
within.

00:03:26.099 --> 00:03:30.660
For obvious reasons, the Foundation doesn’t
maintain any kind of live visual surveillance

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.550
on 096.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.500
It wouldn’t be worth the risk.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:39.650
But what seemed like an otherwise quiet day
suddenly took a turn for the insane.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:44.689
The monitors began displaying terrifying data,
indicating an imminent containment breach,

00:03:44.689 --> 00:03:49.609
as the wails of the creature within the cube
echoed out through its metal walls.

00:03:49.609 --> 00:03:51.110
Some tried to run.

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:55.650
Others did all they could to engage emergency
procedures, while guards armed with heavy

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:58.220
weaponry rushed into the room.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:02.610
They all knew in their hearts that it wouldn’t
save them, but what else could they do?

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:07.890
A huge dent bulged out from the side of the
cube, then another, before the metal was torn

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:12.359
open like tissue paper as the furious hands
of the Shy Guy began clawing their way through

00:04:12.359 --> 00:04:13.359
it.

00:04:13.359 --> 00:04:18.470
Secondary layers of protection were deployed,
but they didn’t help, 096 just kept ripping

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:20.580
through all the barriers.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:27.169
As everyone in attendance knew: Once it was
in its rage state, nothing could stop it.

00:04:27.169 --> 00:04:28.889
Literally nothing.`

00:04:28.889 --> 00:04:33.110
The guards attempted to fire on the anomaly,
but their bullets did no good.

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:37.740
As the creature burst free, most of the people
in the room had at least momentary visual

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.229
contact with its face.

00:04:39.229 --> 00:04:44.490
In response, Code Lima was declared, and the
entire chamber was flooded with a fast-acting

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:47.669
nerve gas, killing everyone.

00:04:47.669 --> 00:04:50.990
Everyone except for 096 itself of course.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:56.770
Within two minutes, 096 had broken free of
the entire containment site, and began running

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:00.810
through the desert at breakneck speeds towards
its distant target.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:05.050
The Foundation needed to act fast and find
a way to stop it before it hit a population

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:08.080
center where the death toll would skyrocket.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:12.840
Team Echo Romeo were dispatched to pursue
the creature in a heavily-armed attack helicopter

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:19.650
while MTF Tau-1, a task force specializing
in SCP-096 containment and recovery, forged

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:26.430
ahead to identify the anomaly’s target,
designated 096-1, and to move any other civilians

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.130
out of harm’s way.

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:34.400
Dr. Dan was alerted of the disastrous situation
and offered guidance to both teams from afar.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:38.580
Echo Romeo’s chopper pursued 096, barely
able to keep up.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:43.740
Dr. Dan recommended attempting to at least
slow the creature down with heavy arms fire,

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:47.770
even though he knew actually stopping it would
be impossible.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:53.120
A member of the team used a modified XM500
anti-materiel rifle to fire several rounds

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.710
at the creature, but even the shot that passed
directly through its head appeared to have

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.150
no effect on it.

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:02.020
But at least they had a lock on its direction
now.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:08.690
096 always travels in a straight line, directly
towards its target, smashing through any obstacles

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:10.060
in its way.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:15.270
This means its intended direction is relatively
easy to track, and people in the path of its

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:22.280
trajectory are even easier to save - but it’s
a high-pressure job reserved for MTF Tau-1.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:28.699
Tau-1 passed over Echo Romeo and 096 in a
series of eight v-22 Ospreys, hoping beyond

00:06:28.699 --> 00:06:32.860
hope that they could outrun the creature;
since there were several different towns in

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:34.080
its direct path.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:39.910
But, thanks once again to the one and only
Dr. Dan, Echo Romeo and Tau-1 had a secret

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:44.620
weapon that neither team had ever possessed
before: SCRAMBLE.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:49.660
SCRAMBLE was an advanced computer program,
created by Dr. Dan with the help of Dr. Oleksei,

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:55.080
which was coded into microprocessors for modification
into camera feeds and viewing goggles.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:07:00.841
The program had been fed intricate data concerning
every single detail of 096’s face, and as

00:07:00.841 --> 00:07:06.810
the name suggests, when encountering that
visual data in real life it scrambles it beyond

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:07.870
recognition.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:13.840
In theory, it would make it far safer for
operatives to be around SCP-096 without activating

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:15.320
its rage state.

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:16.509
In theory.

00:07:16.509 --> 00:07:19.039
It wasn’t long before disaster struck.

00:07:19.039 --> 00:07:24.330
096 had made its way onto I-40, and had begun
attacking vehicles it encountered, killing

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:26.050
the people inside.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:31.039
By this point, it had already outrun the Echo
Romeo chopper, rendering them essentially

00:07:31.039 --> 00:07:32.039
useless.

00:07:32.039 --> 00:07:36.780
Tau-1 just had to forge ahead along 096’s
trajectory, and try to get as many people

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:43.129
out of the danger zone as possible until 096-1
was located and destroyed by the anomaly.

00:07:43.129 --> 00:07:48.539
Years of training for an awful day like this
had paid off, as the first three towns along

00:07:48.539 --> 00:07:51.770
096’s path were successfully evacuated.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:56.970
The Shy Guy just ran right through all of
them, and no lives were lost.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:08:00.990
The same, however, could not be said for town
number four.

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:05.879
As was standard procedure, Tau-1 had everyone
in town gathered up and blindfolded.

00:08:05.879 --> 00:08:11.470
The entire team in attendance had modified
night vision goggles with SCRAMBLE microprocessors,

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:16.889
so in theory, they were better off than most
from 096 if things went south.

00:08:16.889 --> 00:08:20.250
The Tau-1 members tried in vain to keep everybody
in line.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:25.280
They were threatening to shoot anyone who
dared to remove their blindfold when 096 finally

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:26.280
appeared.

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:30.350
It tripped during its approach, rolling and
shattering through several houses.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:31.939
Chaos erupted.

00:08:31.939 --> 00:08:36.780
Some people instinctively removed their blindfolds
to see what was going on, and panicked members

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:39.490
of Tau-1 began firing into the crowd.

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:44.229
The screams of the civilians and the bursts
of gunfire were all drowned out by the horrific

00:08:44.229 --> 00:08:50.940
wailing of 096 itself as it tore through everyone
and everything to kill the unfortunate souls

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:53.100
who had seen its face.

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:58.790
And given how many had removed their blindfolds
during the initial pandemonium, SCP-096 had

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:02.350
a huge number of the townspeople on its list.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:08.750
096 located and grabbed the original 096-1,
the person that’d first glimpsed its face

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:14.230
and caused all this, but in the grand scheme
of things, he was just one more body on the

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:15.950
pile that day.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:22.090
Though of course, we mean this in a purely
metaphorical sense - 096 never leaves entire

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:23.279
bodies.

00:09:23.279 --> 00:09:26.920
The Foundation operatives in attendance were
able to figure out what had caused all this

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:28.940
madness and death.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:34.850
096-1 had been an amateur mountaineer, and
spent his vacations hiking around any mountain

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:40.029
ranges he could gain access to - including
the mountain range that 096 had been inhabiting

00:09:40.029 --> 00:09:43.019
prior to its initial capture and containment.

00:09:43.019 --> 00:09:49.170
But he hadn’t actually seen 096 on that
fateful trip, which he had taken over a decade

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:50.170
ago.

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:56.510
But in a photograph taken that day of himself,
standing on a picturesque mountainside, 096

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:57.890
made a cameo.

00:09:57.890 --> 00:10:04.190
It took up all of four pixels, a tiny off-white
dot against the snow on the back-right side

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:05.750
of the photograph.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:11.100
This photograph, with all the deadly potency
of an atom bomb, had been sitting there for

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:12.170
years.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.240
Waiting.

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:17.260
When the mountaineer was looking through old
photos that morning and his eyes passed over

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:22.740
those few blurry pixels, he didn’t have
any idea that he had just laid his eyes on

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:26.860
one of the most dangerous anomalies the world
has ever seen.

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:29.110
But you don’t have to know.

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:31.490
Only 096 does.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:37.110
As Tau-1, led by their commander, Major Jack
Wilford, tried to retake control of the situation,

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:38.810
things got even worse.

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:43.100
It turned out, Dr. Dan’s SCRAMBLE technology
- the one thing that was supposed to have

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:47.850
given them an edge in this situation - didn’t
actually work.

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:53.019
As soon as goggle wearing members of the team
laid eyes on 096, it entered its rage state

00:10:53.019 --> 00:10:55.190
and started massacring them.

00:10:55.190 --> 00:11:00.070
It tore many of the Mobile Task Force members
to shreds, including a number of the operatives

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:02.800
required for piloting the eight Ospreys.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:08.250
It was a disaster of truly epic proportions,
and the catastrophic failure of Dr. Dan’s

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:10.959
SCRAMBLE technology was a key factor.

00:11:10.959 --> 00:11:14.370
The root of the technology’s failure was
easy enough to figure out.

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:19.830
Dr. Dan’s SCRAMBLE microprocessors worked
fast, but not fast enough.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:24.800
Fractions-of-a-second glimpses of 096’s
face managed to get through, and that was

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:28.399
more than enough to set 096 off.

00:11:28.399 --> 00:11:32.350
Echo Romeo and MTF Epsilon arrived shortly
afterwards to clean up the mess.

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:37.260
It’d been a disaster of such magnitude that
even a CNN reporter arrived on the scene and

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:41.190
started filming before being promptly shut
down by Epsilon.

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:46.339
It was a member of Echo Romeo that finally
slipped the bag over a docile 096’s head,

00:11:46.339 --> 00:11:51.540
preparing it for containment once again, the
creature now content that it had eliminated

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:55.079
all of the unfortunate souls who had seen
its face.

00:11:55.079 --> 00:12:00.889
He’d found 096 sitting next to a minivan
that had its roof ripped off, the young family

00:12:00.889 --> 00:12:04.760
inside being the last to have seen its face.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:09.010
Things were so awful in the aftermath of the
containment breach that the O5 Council changed

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:16.350
their tune, finally granting Dr. Dan permission
to terminate 096, by any means necessary.

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:21.209
It’s terrifying to think that all this can
unfold because of a couple of poorly-timed

00:12:21.209 --> 00:12:22.560
accidents.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:27.139
But it’s probably even more terrifying to
consider that it wasn’t an accident at all.

00:12:27.139 --> 00:12:32.889
It had seemed awfully convenient that both
Dr. Dan and Dr. Oleksei were far from danger

00:12:32.889 --> 00:12:35.170
when all hell broke loose.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:39.810
It was also convenient that, despite the failure
of his technology being a major reason why

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:46.120
the breach was as deadly as it was, Dr. Dan
had still come out of the situation with everything

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.459
he wanted.

00:12:47.459 --> 00:12:52.120
The Foundation also found this strange, and
the more they looked into it, the more they

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.810
found details that didn’t add up.

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:56.970
Alibis began to fall apart.

00:12:56.970 --> 00:13:02.160
Coincidences didn’t seem so coincidental,
and eventually a weak link in the chain was

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:05.610
identified - Dr. Oleksei.

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:09.110
Under pressure from the Foundation, Oleksei
spilled everything.

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:14.651
Dr. Dan had essentially orchestrated the entire
containment breach, and on top of that, he

00:13:14.651 --> 00:13:18.310
did everything he could to make it as deadly
as possible.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:23.899
All with the purpose of getting the O5 Council
to see things his way, and finally give him

00:13:23.899 --> 00:13:30.110
the permission he needed to devote all of
the SCP-096 resources to its termination.

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:34.510
But it came at a terrible price to Dr. Dan
personally.

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:39.000
For his crimes against the Foundation and
humanity, he was permitted to try and figure

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:45.279
out a way to terminate 096 once and for all,
but as payment for his crimes, he himself

00:13:45.279 --> 00:13:49.150
would also be terminated as soon as his task
was complete.

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:54.050
Were the lives of all of those innocent people,
and Dr. Dan’s himself, worth the price of

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:58.279
finally being authorized to terminate SCP-096?

00:13:58.279 --> 00:14:01.720
When asked why he did all this, Dr. Dan simply
said…

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:02.720
“It worked.

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:07.480
There was only a matter of time until that
happened in a major population center, and

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:09.440
its face spread over the world news.

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:14.410
I can kill 096, but I’ve killed myself in
the process.”

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:19.290
While we don’t agree with his methods, there’s
something almost admirable about a person

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:23.220
so single mindedly devoted to their cause.

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:28.889
Now check out “SCP-096 - The Shy Guy”
and “SCP-096 - Look at a Picture of the

00:14:28.889 --> 00:14:30.260
Shy Guy In Space?

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:35.459
The Shy Guy Questions and Theories” if you’re
still itching for another 096 fix!

